   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>Hi,<div><br></div><div>I am working on hidden markov model with rstan.</div><div><br></div><div>As indicated by section 18.2 of stan reference 2.5, label switching hinders the correct estimation of the model frequently.</div><div><br></div><div>In my current model, developed from example code of rstan, the outcome probability density is incorrectly estimated at almost 50% probability and have problem in convergence as well.</div><div><br></div><div>Because I am currently testing with only two hidden state and two outcome probability, the failure would become more significant problem in future.</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve tried to add some code to make an order of state by some parameters (here, prior_alpha) but that solution seems not working well. (the code is attached below.)</div><div><br></div><div>Could anybody suggest a way to add appropriate constraints on the parameters? or to solve label switching problem?</div><div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// num categories</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> V</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// num words</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> I</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// num inds</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> T_unsup</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// num unsupervised items</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">V</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> u</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">I</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T_unsup</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// unsup words</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// transit prior</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">V</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// emit prior</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> age</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">I</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T_unsup</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// covariates for prior probability</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  simplex</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> theta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// transit probs</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  simplex</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">V</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> phi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// emit probs</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> prior_alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// constant for prior prob.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> prior_beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// coefficient for age</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    prior_alpha </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  prior_beta </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    theta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dirichlet</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    phi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dirichlet</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">I</span><span style=\"color:#660\">){</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>    </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// forward algorithm computes log p(u|...)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    real acc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    real gamma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T_unsup</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    real flag</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>    vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> prior</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> priorreg</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>    priorreg </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> prior_alpha </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> prior_beta </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> age</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    prior </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> softmax</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">priorreg</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      gamma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prior</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">phi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">u</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T_unsup</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">j </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>          acc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">j</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> gamma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">j</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">theta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">j</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">phi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">u</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        gamma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> log_sum_exp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">acc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    flag </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      </span><span style=\"color:#008\">if</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prior_alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> prior_alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        flag </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">if</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">flag </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      increment_log_prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">negative_infinity</span><span style=\"color:#660\">());</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">else</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      increment_log_prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">log_sum_exp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">gamma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T_unsup</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]));</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "JRgUJ9mCw3wJ",
   "from": "Bob Carpenter",
   "author": "8aa9b8cc06fdc99c",
   "date": "2014-11-19T22:37:22Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] Adding parameter constraints in order to avoid label switching problem",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>&gt; On Nov 18, 2014, at 7:54 AM, Chanhee Lee &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">face...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Hi,\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I am working on hidden markov model with rstan.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; As indicated by section 18.2 of stan reference 2.5, label switching hinders the correct estimation of the model frequently.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "Label switching shouldn&#39;t affect estimation, just the\r<br>convergence monitoring.  \r<br>\r<br>The real problem is multimodality if you don&#39;t have\r<br>the states associated with your observations.\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>&gt; In my current model, developed from example code of rstan, the outcome probability density is incorrectly estimated at almost 50% probability and have problem in convergence as well.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "See above.  Does it work if you run just one chain for a long time\r<br>(up to label ID, that is)?\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>&gt; Because I am currently testing with only two hidden state and two outcome probability, the failure would become more significant problem in future.\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I&#39;ve tried to add some code to make an order of state by some parameters (here, prior_alpha) but that solution seems not working well. (the code is attached below.)\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "I don&#39;t think this is a good solution in general, because\r<br>you probably don&#39;t want to have such an ordering as part of\r<br>the model.\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>&gt; Could anybody suggest a way to add appropriate constraints on the parameters? or to solve label switching problem?\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "There&#39;s not a good general solution here.  If the states\r<br>are highly separated you can reidentify with the posterior\r<br>by matching the estimates, but that won&#39;t help with multimodality.\r<br>\r<br>- Bob\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
